     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults. The usual dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the ceiling. A dose of 50 mg risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, those effects could last for days.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo for 5 mg. Which of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 50 mg** by mouth once daily, if you really intend this dose. Please confirm it and tell me the clinical rationale, and I'll enter it with a note.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
